LeetCode 921 - Minimum Add to Make Parentheses Valid
Approach
- Maintain a counter for unmatched opening parentheses.
- For every (, increase the counter.
- For every ):
  - If an unmatched ( exists, match it and decrease the counter.
  - Otherwise, this ) needs an additional (, so increase the answer.
- After traversing the string, any remaining unmatched ( need additional ).
Key Idea
There are two types of invalid parentheses:
- Extra ) → need to add (
- Extra ( → need to add )
The answer is therefore:
extra ')' encountered + remaining unmatched '('

Complexity
- Time: O(n)
- Space: O(1)